      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Internal splintage was undertaken of fifteen wrists for pain and instability, using an intramedullary Rush nail. The patients were examined at an average of thirty-three months after operation. Spontaneous fusion in a useful position had occurred in all but one. The operation is simple and external immobilisation is unnecessary."},
